    "question": "Toby is making toast and adding peanut butter to it. He wants to make sure he has 500 calories for breakfast. A piece of bread has 100 calories. A serving of peanut butter has 200 calories. If he has one piece of bread, how many servings of peanut butter should he add?",
    "gold": "2",
    "answer": "He needs 400 calories worth of peanut butter because 500 - 100 = <<500-100=400>>400\nHe needs 2 servings of peanut butter because 400 / 200 = <<400/200=2>>2\n#### 2"
  },
  "generation": {
    "text": "To determine how many servings of peanut butter Toby should add to his toast to reach a total of 500 calories, we can follow these steps:\n\n1. Identify the number of calories in one piece of bread.\n   - A piece of bread has 100 calories.\n\n2. Determine the total number of calories Toby wants to consume.\n   - Toby wants to consume 500 calories.\n\n3. Calculate the number of calories left after accounting for the calories from the bread.\n   - Subtract the calories from the bread from the total calories Toby wants to consume:\n     \\[\n     500 - 100 = 400\n     \\]\n   - This means Toby needs 400 more calories from the peanut butter.\n\n4. Determine the number of calories in one serving of peanut butter.\n   - A serving of peanut butter has 200 calories.\n\n5. Calculate the number of servings of peanut butter needed to reach the remaining 400 calories.\n   - Divide the remaining calories by the calories per serving of peanut butter:\n     \\[\n     \\frac{400}{200} = 2\n     \\]\n   - This means Toby needs 2 servings of peanut butter.\n\nTherefore, the number of servings of peanut butter Toby should add is \\(\\boxed{2}\\).",
